From f724d09fc91bb060ab3aeea1e66067501674fd53 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 22:00:56 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 21/53] System dialogs drawn as a band over the game

The message dialog and the save-data dialog are the game's, opened over a
running game, not the port's menus: they now sit in a translucent band
across the screen (widgets.hpp, band::) with white text centred in it, a
soft highlight on the selected choice and the button hints at the band's
lower right, in the spirit of the handheld's own dialogs. The save list
shows the slots down the left and the selected save's title, detail and
date on the right. Original drawing and colours; no console assets and no
code from other projects.

hints() takes an optional style (the band's is kBandHints), hints_width()
measures, and draw_band() and draw_choice() draw the band and the
highlight. The menus' own look is unchanged. Input, answers and results
are as before.

Verified on Windows with one game: its autosave notice, a yes/no
question, the load list and its confirmation, and the save list, with a
virtual pad. Not verified: the mouse and touch in these dialogs, very
narrow windows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
